# PaInheritanceTaxCharge — Pennsylvania inheritance tax charge (72 P.S. § 9116)

The Pennsylvania inheritance tax charge on one beneficiary's share of a decedent's estate,
per 72 P.S. § 9116(a). Like Ireland CAT and unlike UK Inheritance Tax, this is
**beneficiary-side**: the rate is keyed to the beneficiary's relationship to the decedent, so
the scope takes one invocation per (beneficiary x share) — the incidence nuance is that the
rate is recipient-keyed even though the estate's personal representative files the return
(REV-1500) and remits the tax; the machine-readable incidence axis lives in the jurisdiction
parameter layer (`linkml/parameters/parameters.yaml` `TaxIncidenceEnum`), not in Catala.

The scope returns the `ComputedOrNeedsHuman.Verdict` contract (doctrine §1a; Constitution
Principle XIII): a definite legal figure travels in the `Computed` arm.

Legal-correctness is asserted **outside this file** by the T032 gov-oracle harness (TT-478):
`code-inherit-test-suite/scripts/oracle_verify.py` runs this scope and checks the computed
figure against the published revenue.pa.gov figure cited in
`tests/oracles/pa-inheritance-tax.oracle.json`. This file therefore carries the law, not its
own assertions.

(Prose note: a line must not begin with the reserved `>` directive prefix, so any statutory
quotation is kept inline.)

Statutory rates (current values; live-sourced revenue.pa.gov 2026-07-02, 72 P.S. § 9116(a)):

- 0% on transfers to a surviving spouse, or to a parent from a child aged 21 or younger
- 4.5% on transfers to direct descendants and lineal heirs
- 12% on transfers to siblings
- 15% on transfers to other heirs (except charitable organisations, exempt institutions, and
  government entities exempt from tax)

There is **no threshold** — PA inheritance tax is charged from the first dollar of the taxable
share (unlike Ireland CAT's group thresholds). The family exemption (20 Pa.C.S. § 3121, $3,500)
and § 9111 exemptions are not computed by this rule — a claimed deduction or exemption routes
to `NeedsHuman` (`deduction_or_exemption_claimed`); so does the 5% prepayment discount for
payment within three months of death, which reduces the amount due rather than the rate.

The per-class rates are `context` parameters (ICP-A1) whose authoritative values live in the
jurisdiction parameter layer; the literals below are the overridable defaults. The 0% classes
are structural (not merely a zero-valued context parameter) because they are exemptions in
their own right, not a rate that happens to be zero.

G6 certification floor (TT-427/TT-1079): every input is a characterisation judgement
(`registry/governance-layers.yaml`, all L3 — the share valuation, the beneficiary-class
relationship classification, and the deduction/exemption claim), so each arrives as a
`Certified<Type> | NotCharacterised` enum; any uncertified input routes `NeedsHuman`
via the `uncertified_inputs` gate. `CertifiedPaBeneficiaryClass` is declared HERE (the
rule-local twin of this module's own classification enum — the shared contract module
cannot import rule modules).

```catala
declaration enumeration PaBeneficiaryClass:
  -- SurvivingSpouse
  -- ChildUnder21ToParent
  -- LinealHeir
  -- Sibling
  -- Collateral
  -- ExemptCharityOrGovernment

declaration enumeration CertifiedPaBeneficiaryClass:
  -- Certified content PaBeneficiaryClass
  -- NotCharacterised

declaration scope Charge:
  input taxable_value content ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney
  input beneficiary_class content CertifiedPaBeneficiaryClass
  input deduction_or_exemption_claimed content ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool
  context rate_lineal content decimal
  context rate_sibling content decimal
  context rate_collateral content decimal
  internal uncertified_inputs content boolean
  internal taxable_value_v content money
  internal beneficiary_class_v content PaBeneficiaryClass
  internal deduction_or_exemption_claimed_v content boolean
  output verdict content ComputedOrNeedsHuman.Verdict

scope Charge:
  definition rate_lineal equals 0.045
  definition rate_sibling equals 0.12
  definition rate_collateral equals 0.15
  definition uncertified_inputs equals
    (match taxable_value with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.Certified content v: false -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.NotCharacterised: true)
    or (match beneficiary_class with pattern -- CertifiedPaBeneficiaryClass.Certified content v: false -- CertifiedPaBeneficiaryClass.NotCharacterised: true)
    or (match deduction_or_exemption_claimed with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content v: false -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.NotCharacterised: true)
  # certified-value extractions — fallbacks are dead code (verdict routes first)
  definition taxable_value_v equals
    match taxable_value with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.Certified content v: v -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.NotCharacterised: $0
  definition beneficiary_class_v equals
    match beneficiary_class with pattern -- CertifiedPaBeneficiaryClass.Certified content v: v -- CertifiedPaBeneficiaryClass.NotCharacterised: Collateral
  definition deduction_or_exemption_claimed_v equals
    match deduction_or_exemption_claimed with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content v: v -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.NotCharacterised: false
  definition verdict equals
    if uncertified_inputs then
      NeedsHuman
    else if deduction_or_exemption_claimed_v then
      NeedsHuman
    else
      match beneficiary_class_v with pattern
      -- SurvivingSpouse: Computed content $0
      -- ChildUnder21ToParent: Computed content $0
      -- ExemptCharityOrGovernment: Computed content $0
      -- LinealHeir: Computed content (taxable_value_v * rate_lineal)
      -- Sibling: Computed content (taxable_value_v * rate_sibling)
      -- Collateral: Computed content (taxable_value_v * rate_collateral)
```
